{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": [
    "THE single definition of every alert type. Read at RUNTIME by the backend,",
    "the Discord bot and (via GET /api/dashboard/alert-catalog) the dashboard.",
    "",
    "Read at runtime, not compiled in, on purpose: a git pull updates this file",
    "whether or not anything rebuilt. A stale dist used to mean the API rejected",
    "keys the dashboard offered, which surfaced as bad_request on every save.",
    "",
    "Naming rule: the key names the AGENCY, the suffix names the stream.",
    "So qfd/qfd_warning and dfes/dfes_warning, never qld_*/wa_*.",
    "",
    "archiveSource is the data_history `source` value and is deliberately",
    "many-types-to-one: the five Victorian agencies all carry vic_emergency.",
    "The logs page groups by archiveSource; Discord alerts key on `key`.",
    "",
    "endpoint is what the bot polls. A feed on /api/v1/ is polled there; the",
    "per-agency fire incident and warning feeds and The Wire are not on",
    "/api/v1/ and stay on /api/.",
    "/api/v1/ wraps a body that is not GeoJSON in {data: ...}, so itemsPath",
    "is a dotted path into it ('data.warnings'; 'data' for a bare list).",
    "",
    "feedShape outage_v1 is the merged outage feed (/api/v1/outages), one type",
    "per distributor outside NSW. Its endpoint asks for status=active only:",
    "the bot announces every record it has not seen, and a distributor lists",
    "hundreds of planned jobs that have not started. Planned work is announced",
    "when it starts.",
    "",
    "state is the one state every record of a type is in (NSW, VIC, QLD, SA,",
    "WA, TAS, NT or ACT), for a preset's States filter. Leave it off a type",
    "whose records span states (BOM, FIRMS, shark reports, pager, The Wire):",
    "a record's own properties.state wins when it has one, and an alert whose",
    "state is unknown passes the filter rather than being dropped."
  ],

  "_severityComment": [
    "A scale owns everything about reading a severity: WHERE the raw value is",
    "on a record (field), what the floor options are (options, worst last),",
    "and how upstream's wording maps onto them (map, matched lowercased).",
    "An unmapped raw value means 'no severity available' and the floor passes",
    "rather than blocking — never drop an alert over missing metadata."
  ],
  "severityScales": {
    "fire": {
      "field": "properties.alertLevel",
      "options": [
        { "value": "advice", "label": "Advice" },
        { "value": "watch_and_act", "label": "Watch & Act" },
        { "value": "emergency", "label": "Emergency" }
      ],
      "map": {
        "advice": "advice",
        "watch and act": "watch_and_act",
        "watch_and_act": "watch_and_act",
        "emergency warning": "emergency",
        "emergency": "emergency",
        "not applicable": "__below__"
      }
    },
    "bom": {
      "field": "severity",
      "options": [
        { "value": "minor", "label": "Minor" },
        { "value": "moderate", "label": "Moderate" },
        { "value": "major", "label": "Major" }
      ],
      "map": {
        "severe": "major", "warning": "moderate", "watch": "moderate",
        "advice": "minor", "info": "minor",
        "minor": "minor", "moderate": "moderate", "major": "major"
      }
    }
  },

